From 44354a387f996a7685c9b2debad03fa9a3361e50 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CharlesWu <296364977+charxwu@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 17:36:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] fix(simple_kv_offload): align CPU offload pool size
 across PP workers

Under pipeline parallelism or spec decode, SimpleCPUOffload workers on
different ranks can derive different num_cpu_blocks from their local KV
tensor layouts while the scheduler assigns a shared cpu_block_id space.
Align worker pool sizes via world-group MIN all-reduce on live tensor
strides, collect the value in the engine after KV cache registration,
and size the scheduler pool from that aligned count.

Signed-off-by: CharlesWu <296364977+charxwu@users.noreply.github.com>
---
